values ('6b295ff7-237c-5b5e-aacc-7ca2c2cbbb3d', 'rg3-word-parts-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Rainy Game$q$, $q$The Comets soccer team had a big game on Saturday. Rain fell all morning, and the field was muddy and slippery. Kenji and Talia, who are teammates, waited under a tent with the rest of the team.

"Maybe the game will be canceled," Kenji said. Talia disagreed. "The rain is getting lighter. I think we will play."

Talia was right. The referee said the field was playable. The players ran out, but the ball kept sliding in the mud. Kenji kicked it hard, and it rolled the wrong way. Kenji had misjudged how fast the ball would move on the wet grass.

At halftime, the Comets were losing by one goal. Coach Delgado gathered the team. "Do not worry about the mud," the coach said. "Take small steps and pass the ball softly."

In the second half, the Comets played carefully. Talia passed the ball to Kenji, and Kenji scored! The game ended in a tie. The players were muddy from head to toe, but nobody was unhappy. It had been a wonderful, messy day.$q$, 'draft')
