-- Passage rg3-word-parts-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f4d5169c-9aee-55a5-9b4a-0a44d09c886e', 'rg3-word-parts-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Kites in the Sky$q$, $q$People have been flying kites for a very long time. Many experts think the first kites were made in China more than two thousand years ago.

A kite needs wind to fly. On a breezy day, the moving air pushes up on the kite and lifts it into the sky. When there is no wind at all, a kite is unable to stay up, and it falls to the ground.

Many kites are colorful. Some are bright red, yellow and blue. Others look like birds, fish or dragons. Bright colors make a kite easy to see high above.

A long tail can be useful, too. The tail helps keep the kite steady so it does not spin in circles.

Kite flying is fun, but it must be done with care. A kite in an open field is harmless. A kite near power lines is not, because the string can touch the wires. Always fly a kite far away from wires, roads and trees.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
