insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('27a59783-2e8d-5f9d-bdae-5045ea0f13f2', 'rg3-word-parts-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Clay Bowl$q$, $q$On Tuesday, the art club tried something new. Ms. Ferreira set a lump of wet clay in front of each student. "Today we are making bowls," she said.

Rohan had never touched clay before. It felt cold and sticky, and at first Rohan was uncomfortable with the mess. Rohan's friend Esi laughed. "Clay is supposed to be messy. That is the fun part!"

Rohan pressed a thumb into the middle of the clay and began to pinch the sides. The bowl came out lopsided. Ms. Ferreira showed Rohan how to reshape it. "Wet your fingers and smooth the edge slowly," she said.

The second try was much better. Rohan worked carefully, turning the bowl a little at a time. Soon the bowl had round, even sides.

Next week, the bowls will be baked in a hot oven called a kiln. Then the students will paint them. Esi wants to paint stars. Rohan plans to paint blue waves and give the bowl to Grandpa. In one afternoon, Rohan had gone from a nervous beginner to a proud artist.$q$, 'draft')
