-- Passage rg4-authors-purpose-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('77c71ca8-3ec9-5da5-b547-b1e7a2f7e617', 'rg4-authors-purpose-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Championship Game$q$, $q$Account 1: A Blog Post by Priya Nair, Team Captain

Last night my team, the Riverside Rollers, played in the state wheelchair basketball final. My arms were tired from pushing up and down the court, but I kept going. With ten seconds left, we were behind by one point. Coach called a time-out and drew a play on her clipboard. Jada passed me the ball, and I took a shot from the corner. It bounced on the rim twice before it dropped in! The crowd was so loud I couldn't hear myself yell. We won by one point. I still can't stop smiling.

Account 2: From the Sports Page of the Riverside Daily News

The Riverside Rollers won the state youth wheelchair basketball title on Friday. They beat the Hillcrest Hawks by a score of 42 to 41. The Rollers trailed for most of the game, and Hillcrest led by eight points at halftime. Riverside cut the lead in the second half thanks to strong defense. Captain Priya Nair scored the winning basket in the final seconds and finished with 14 points. It is the team's first state title since the league began twelve years ago. The team will be honored at a town meeting next month.$q$, 'draft')
