-- Passage rg4-authors-purpose-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4123252c-34b0-5bc6-88ed-62a20811c52e', 'rg4-authors-purpose-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The House That Rolled Down Main Street$q$, $q$Account 1: An Email from Keiko Tanaka to Her Friend

Hi Rosa,

You will not believe what I saw this morning. A whole house rolled right past my front window! It was the old yellow house from the corner of Main and Elm. Workers had lifted it onto a giant trailer with about twenty wheels. It moved slower than a person walking. A worker on a ladder held up the traffic light wires so the roof could pass under them. My little brother waved at the house like it was a parade float. Our street was closed all morning, so Mom had to walk to work.

Talk soon, Keiko

Account 2: From the Town of Fairmont Website

On Saturday, the historic Gable House was moved four blocks to its new home on Lake Street. The house was built in 1885. It is one of the oldest buildings in Fairmont. It was moved to make room for a new fire station at its old spot. The move took about five hours. Crews raised wires and trimmed tree branches along the route. The Fairmont History Club plans to turn the house into a small museum next year. The town thanks neighbors for their patience while roads were closed.$q$, 'draft')
