   $q$How is the way leaves turn red different from the way they turn yellow?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Red comes from chlorophyll, but yellow comes from sugar.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-details"},{"text":"Red is made new in fall, but yellow was there all summer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Yellow is made new in fall, but red was there all summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-relationship"},{"text":"Red shows up only on cloudy days with very warm nights.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Red is made new in fall, but yellow was there all summer.$q$, $q$Paragraph 4 says, "Red colors are not in the leaf all summer," and trees make red in the fall, while paragraph 3 says yellow was hiding all summer. The choice "Yellow is made new in fall, but red was there all summer" flips this connection around.$q$, 'draft', '7883d06a-43bc-50ce-a96b-b91f6a5303b1')
