   $q$A student's bowl cracks in the kiln, even though it dried slowly. Based on the passage, what is the most likely cause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The glaze on the bowl was brushed on much too shiny.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The student kept wet hands while shaping on the wheel.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-relationship"},{"text":"The bowl went through two firings instead of only one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-process"},{"text":"The clay was not wedged well, so air stayed trapped inside.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The clay was not wedged well, so air stayed trapped inside.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 says trapped air "can expand in the hot kiln and crack the pot," and slow drying rules out the other crack cause in paragraph 4. Wet hands are a correct step that keeps clay from tearing, not a cause of cracks.$q$, 'draft', 'f620bbae-f9c6-5c53-bd40-72fd4f3b3070')
