-- Passage rg4-connections-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1815c1c0-32f8-5d9d-9c20-13a66ba7154d', 'rg4-connections-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-connections'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Lights Out for Baby Turtles$q$, $q$On warm summer nights, baby sea turtles hatch from eggs buried in the sand. Each hatchling is small enough to fit in your hand. As soon as it climbs out of its nest, it has one job: reach the ocean.

How does a hatchling know which way to go? It looks for the brightest direction. On a natural beach, the open sky over the ocean is brighter than the land behind the beach, where trees and dunes block the light. So the hatchlings crawl toward the glow, and the glow leads them to the water.

Bright lights from buildings can cause a problem. Porch lights, streetlights and hotel windows can shine brighter than the sky over the sea. Hatchlings may crawl toward these lights instead. They can end up lost on roads or in parking lots, far from the ocean.

In the beach town of Palmetto Shores, people decided to help. During nesting season, families close their curtains at night. Streetlights near the beach were changed to dim, low lights that point down at the ground. Volunteers walk the beach at sunrise and mark new nests with small flags.

The changes worked. Volunteers now find far fewer hatchlings wandering away from the water. More of the tiny turtles reach the waves and begin their long lives at sea.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
