-- Passage rg4-evidence-inference-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f1b172c0-80e2-542b-9287-2deb5083d135', 'rg4-evidence-inference-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-evidence-inference'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Wheelchair Basketball$q$, $q$Wheelchair basketball is a fast and exciting team sport. Players use special wheelchairs instead of running up and down the court. The court, the hoop and the ball are the same size as in other basketball games.

The chairs are built just for this sport. Their wheels tilt inward at the bottom. This shape helps players turn quickly without tipping over. A small extra wheel at the back keeps the chair steady. Many chairs also have a bar in front to protect the players' feet.

Players must push their wheels and handle the ball at the same time. A player may push the wheels twice while holding the ball. After that, the player must pass, shoot or bounce the ball. Strong arms and quick hands are very important.

Teams practice many hours each week. They work on passing, shooting and moving their chairs into open spaces. Some teams include players with and without disabilities. Today, wheelchair basketball is played in many countries. Top players even compete in a large international sports event every four years.$q$, 'draft')
