insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('850166be-003a-5eff-9d28-85c31ec646df', 'rg4-evidence-inference-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-evidence-inference'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Every Student Should Learn to Swim$q$, $q$I believe every student in our town should learn to swim before fifth grade. Swimming is a skill that keeps people safe, and it is also a lot of fun.

First, swimming helps people stay safe near water. Our town sits next to a lake, and many families go boating in the summer. A child who can swim and float is better prepared if he or she falls in. Knowing how to swim also helps a person stay calm in the water.

Second, swimming is great exercise. It makes the heart and lungs stronger. It works the arms, the legs and the belly muscles all at once. People of almost any age can swim, so it is a skill that lasts a whole life.

Some people say lessons cost too much. However, the town pool already has an empty hour every weekday morning. The school could use that time for free classes taught by the pool's lifeguards.

When I learned to swim, I was nervous at first. By the end of the lessons, I was jumping off the side of the pool. Every student deserves to feel that proud.$q$, 'draft')
