   $q$At the end, Omar remembers the saying "Little by little, a little becomes a lot." Why does this saying fit his day?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He needs to draw only small pictures in his sketchbook.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"One new friend is a small start that can grow into more.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He should not try to make friends until he is older.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He has already made a lot of friends on his first day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-extreme"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$One new friend is a small start that can grow into more.$q$, $q$The passage says "He had made one friend" right before the saying, which is a small step that can add up over time. He has not made many friends yet, so the saying is about growing, not about having a lot already.$q$, 'draft', 'b8088318-cdfd-53d8-a11f-968358a5c2b2')
