   $q$Why does the poet repeat the line "Clack and clatter, clack and hum" at the beginning and the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that the train broke down and had to start its trip over","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To tell the reader the exact time when the train left the station","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"To introduce a new character who rides the train at the very end","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To echo the steady sound of the train and close the poem the way it began","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To echo the steady sound of the train and close the poem the way it began$q$, $q$The repeated line sounds like train wheels, and using it first and last makes the poem feel like one full trip from start to finish. Nothing in the poem says the train broke down.$q$, 'draft', '6f32f95f-8a6f-56d9-8d01-4caba2f9dc74')
