   $q$Which statement best describes the narrator of this fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The hummingbird, who tells the story using \"I\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-first-and-third-person"},{"text":"An outside narrator who calls the birds \"he\" and \"she\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"A bee, who watches the birds from the flowers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The heron, who tells the story using \"I\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-first-and-third-person"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An outside narrator who calls the birds "he" and "she"$q$, $q$The narrator is not one of the animals and uses "he" for the heron and "she" for the hummingbird, which is third person. The birds only say "I" inside their spoken lines.$q$, 'draft', '60431ae8-50d8-5029-856d-eb8f1056461c')
